  "Number": 7,
  "Question": "A triangle has side lengths \\(10,\\) \\(10,\\) and \\(12.\\) A rectangle has width \\(4\\) and area equal to the area of the triangle. What is the perimeter of this rectangle?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(16\\)",
    "B": "\\(24\\)",
    "C": "\\(28\\)",
    "D": "\\(32\\)",
    "E": "\\(36\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The two equal sides suggest drawing the altitude to the side of length \\(12\\). In an isosceles triangle, this altitude bisects the base, producing two right triangles with a leg of length \\(6\\) and hypotenuse \\(10\\).\n\nLet \\(h>0\\) be the altitude. The Pythagorean theorem gives\n\\[h^2+6^2=10^2,\\qquad h^2=64,\\qquad h=8.\\]\nThus the triangle's area is\n\\[\\frac12\\cdot12\\cdot8=48.\\]\nThe rectangle has the same area and width \\(4\\), so its length is \\(48\\div4=12\\). Its perimeter is therefore\n\\[2(12+4)=\\boxed{32},\\]\nwhich is choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
